{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pre-merge Windows check of the full stack passed. The stack is undamaging-ashamed-wasp → flowered-nonvalued-mink → inaccurate-genetic-asianlion → this change. Throwaway branch `w1-diag-opcert-acl` at 18cdfe2ff80, `sweep (windows)` run 44606991897, job 135853215223, conclusion success. The 28 former `openssh-key-acl.args` tests, plus the new tests of all 4 tickets: 44 passed, 1 skipped (the POSIX-only test). inaccurate-genetic-asianlion is the third defect found here: on Windows, op-cert job workspaces leaked because `discard`'s rmtree cannot delete git's read-only objects. That leak was the last cause of the nested leak test failing. The stack lands in that order so the main sweep stays green. `make verify` is running on the stack tip."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795119623116035883,"uuid":"9a332736-2035-4a48-8fff-33aa73272586"}